    metric "Getting started" "Quick start" "Link pico.css manually or via CDN for a dependency-free setup, or use NPM or Composer for advanced usage."
    col
      text Content
      link "Install manually" /docs#install-manually
      link "Usage from CDN" /docs#usage-from-cdn
      link "Install with NPM" /docs#install-with-npm
      link "Install with Composer" /docs#install-with-composer
      link "Starter HTML template" /docs#starter-html-template
    col
      text There are 4 ways to get started with pico.css:
      h2 Install manually#
      text and link  in the  of your website.
      row
        link "Download Pico" https://github.com/picocss/pico/archive/refs/heads/main.zip
        text /css/pico.min.css
        text <head>
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs
        text "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/pico.min.css\">"
      h2 Usage from CDN#
      text Alternatively, you can use  to link.
      row
        link "jsDelivr CDN" https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@picocss/pico@2/
        text pico.min.css
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs
        text "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@picocss/pico@2/css/pico.min.css\" >"
      h2 Install with NPM#
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs
        text npm install @picocss/pico
      text Or
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs
        text yarn add @picocss/pico
      text Then, import Pico into your SCSS file with :
      link "@use" https://sass-lang.com/documentation/at-rules/use
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs
        text "@use \"pico\";"
      text Learn more about the .
      link "customization with Sass" /docs/sass
      h2 Install with Composer#
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs
        text composer require picocss/pico
      h2 Starter HTML template#
      card
        link "Copy code" /docs
        text "<!doctype html> <html lang=\"en\"> <head> <meta charset=\"utf-8\"> <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"> <meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"> <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"css/pico.min.css\"> <title>Hello world!</title> </head> <body> <main class=\"container\"> <h1>Hello world!</h1> </main> </body> </html>"
      link "Edit this page on GitHub" https://github.com/picocss/picocss.com/blob/main/app/routes/docs._index.jsx
